# Build output at any depth, not just the root `dist` above. Every image builds
# what it needs inside itself, so a host-built `apps/*/dist` in the context is
# never used on purpose, only by accident, and that accident makes a build pass
# on a developer's machine and fail from a clean checkout.
**/dist

# Tests and browser specs have no business in a production image. Excluding them
# is load-bearing rather than tidiness: Next type-checks every file its tsconfig
# includes, so a spec reaching for a dependency the app deliberately does not
# declare would fail the image build.
**/e2e
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
